Sylvester Stallone 's classic film &#x201C; Rocky &#x201D; premiered half a century ago.

To mark the occasion, artist John Rivoli has released a new book, &#x201C;The Fine Art Of Rocky: An Artistic Tribute From Screen To Canvas,&#x201D; published by Insight Editions.

The book features rare and never-before-seen original Rocky paintings by Rivoli, an official MGM/Amazon Rocky artist. Related Stories Jeff Goldblum Breaks Into 'Wicked' Song While Reflecting on His 'Unexpectedly Enduring Career' at Marrakech: 'You Just Follow Your Curiosity and Your Heart' How 'Backrooms' Artisans Transformed YouTube Series Into Cinema’s Favorite Liminal Space Using 30,000 Square Feet of Sets and Four Sound Stages

Part art book and part analysis of the six Rocky films, the book invites fans to revisit the iconic franchise through Rivoli&#x2019;s collection of large-scale original paintings and iconic posters, seeing the beloved character in a whole new light. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Rocky takes center stage in this deluxe book, with over 70 of Rivoli's paintings, posters and other unique artworks highlighting unforgettable moments from the films presented in original and unique perspectives as well as art collaborations with Stallone.

Rivoli said, &#x201C;This book represents a lifetime of training &#x2014; for this moment, for this story, for this opportunity to reinterpret Rocky through my own artistic lens.&#x201D;

Speaking with Variety, Rivoli pointed to two pieces featured in the book. The first, &#x201C;Alone in the Ring,&#x201D; is something that holds a special place in his heart. &#x201C;I struggled with how to tell this story visually. I knew that to capture the true significance of the moment, I had to make Rocky small on the canvas. As an artist, that&#x2019;s a difficult decision when you know collectors want a large, commanding image of Rocky hanging on their walls.&#x201D;

Rivoli says the painting wasn&#x2019;t about making Rocky larger than life. &#x201C;It was about showing him surrounded by something much bigger than himself. The ring is enormous, the arena is vast, and the towering image of Apollo Creed dominates the space. Everything around Rocky is larger than he is, emphasizing just how small and alone he feels in that moment.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

It's also a turning point in the film as Rocky's goal shifts from wanting to win the fight to something far more meaningful: going the distance and proving to himself that he&#x2019;s not just another bum from the neighborhood.

&#x201C;That realization is the emotional heart of the story, and it&#x2019;s what I wanted the painting to communicate.&#x201D;

Another meaningful work of art is &#x201C;The Chosen One.&#x201D; Rivoli reveals the original hangs in Stallone's home. He says, &#x201C;It captures the very foundation of the film and the character study that Sylvester Stallone so brilliantly establishes in its opening moments. 'Rocky' begins with an image of Jesus. The camera slowly pans down, revealing the word 'Resurrection,' before ultimately introducing us to Rocky Balboa. In that beautifully constructed sequence, we&#x2019;re being told something profound: we&#x2019;re about to witness the resurrection or redemption of this man.&#x201D; He adds, &#x201C;I find that moment incredibly powerful and I wanted to capture its spiritual and emotional significance on canvas.&#x201D;

&#x201C;My hope is that readers don&#x2019;t just experience the film again, but feel it in a way they never have before &#x2014; as if they&#x2019;re seeing Rocky for the very first time. If it moves them, if it reveals something new, then I&#x2019;ve done what I set out to do.&#x201D;

This richly illustrated volume reimagines Rocky as an immersive artistic celebration, bringing moments from screen to canvas, which invites fans to experience the iconic character in a bold new light across his 50-year legacy.

Guitarist Andy Taylor , whose tenure in England&#x2019;s glammy, pop-savvy rock band Duran Duran coincided with the group&#x2019;s commercial pinnacle of the early &#x2018;80s, died of prostate cancer at his home on Monday while surrounded by family. He was 65.

In a statement shared with Variety , Taylor's wife Tracey said on behalf of their family, "To the world, Andy was a brilliant guitarist, but to us, he was the most wonderful husband, a loving dad and the proudest grandfather. He was the rock of our family. For all the incredible experiences music brought him, family always came first. Nothing made him happier than having us all together, and no matter how far music took him, his heart was always at home." blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories David Fincher Explains AI Use in ‘Cliff Booth’ and How AI Can Be Used on Film Sets to Reduce The Amount of Takes but Still Have ‘Real Human Beings’ Vijay Sethupathi's 'Maharaja' Producer Confirms Hollywood Remake Approach as WAVES Film Bazaar Panel Weighs Whether Indian IP Can Travel

Duran Duran added, "Andy was there at the very beginning of our story. From the moment he arrived in Birmingham from the North East with a guitar and an unshakeable belief in what we could become, he brought an indelible fire and swagger to our music. His playing drove the songs that took us around the world, and with a dry wit that was matched only by his wonderfully unsentimental, no-nonsense outlook on life he kept us grounded and gave the band its edge through the extraordinary years that followed."

Taylor, who was diagnosed with stage 4 metastatic prostate cancer in 2018, had opted out on appearing at the group&#x2019;s November 2022 induction into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame, citing a decline in his health in a statement.

He said, &#x201C;Although my current condition is not immediately life-threatening there is no cure&#x2026;. Recently I was doing OK after some very sophisticated life-extending treatment, that was until a week or so ago when I suffered a setback, and despite the exceptional efforts of my team, I had to be honest in that both physically and mentally, I would be pushing my boundaries.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Duran Duran had been in existence for two years in the Midlands city of Birmingham when Taylor &#x2014; then a 19-year-old veteran seeking new opportunities after successfully touring British army bases in Europe with a cover band &#x2014; spotted a April 1980 Melody Maker classified ad seeking a &#x201C;Live Wire Guitarist.&#x201D;

He wrote in &#x201C;Wild Boy,&#x201D; his candid and frequently sensational 2008 autobiography, &#x201C;[The ad] cited Mick Ronson of the Spiders From Mars and Steve Jones of the Sex Pistols as musical influences so I thought it looked worth a call.&#x201D;

After a successful audition, Taylor became a member of the quintet, which became a popular fixture at the Birmingham club the Rum Runner. Sporting extravagant coiffs and makeup &#x2014; &#x201C;We&#x2019;d end up discussing cosmetics with the girls,&#x201D; Taylor later wrote &#x2014; the band was lumped in with Britain&#x2019;s New Romantic movement of the early &#x2018;80s. After only eight months with Taylor in the lineup, the act was signed by EMI.

Duran Duran &#x2014; whose early compositions were credited to all five group members &#x2014; became a nearly instant success in the U.K. Its third single &#x201C;Girls on Film&#x201D; (No. 5) helped push its self-titled debut album to No. 3. The 1982 followup album &#x201C;Riot&#x201D; spawned the hits &#x201C;Hungry Like the Wolf&#x201D; (No. 5) and the eponymous single (No. 9). Its first No. 1 single &#x201C;Is There Something I Should Know&#x201D; was issued in 1983.

The band was among the first beneficiaries of Stateside exposure on MTV, the then-new cable network that broke through with wall-to-wall airing of videos; their lavish clips, handsomely directly by former 10cc members Kevin Godley and Lol Creme and the prolific Russell Mulcahy, captured eyes with their lush cinematography, scantily clad models and expensive location shoots in exotic locales like Sri Lanka and Antigua. Three Duran Duran singles reached the U.S. top five in 1982-83.

Taylor noted in his memoir that those videos often found the band members risking life and limb: &#x201C;They were enormous fun to make &#x2014; even if it nearly killed us at times. I&#x2019;m not joking! Several of us risked being drowned, we narrowly escaped being trampled by a crazed elephant, and we were forced to flee one shoot after being threatened by four thousand angry monks.&#x201D; Unsurprisingly, Duran Duran&#x2019;s only Grammy Awards, both presented in 1986, were for best short form music video and (for &#x201C;Duran Duran,&#x201D; a compilation of their first 12 clips) best long form music video. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

By 1983, the act was big enough in England to headline a London charity benefit attended by Prince Charles and Princess Diana, who told its members, &#x201C;I don&#x2019;t need any introductions to these boys. I know exactly who they are.&#x201D; Their album of that year, Seven and the Ragged Tiger,&#x201D; shot to No. 1 in the U.K. and No. 8 in the U.S.

However, by 1984, when the singles &#x201C;The Reflex&#x201D; and &#x201C;The Wild Boys&#x201D; reached No. 1 and No. 2 respectively in both the U.K. and the U.S., the band&#x2019;s hard-partying, notoriously debauched lifestyle was beginning to shred their reputation; a story in the Fleet Street tabloid the Sun detailed stories of extreme cocaine abuse &#x2014; later verified by Taylor, who, with bassist John Taylor (no relation), was the drug&#x2019;s most enthusiastic user. Additional turmoil came into the guitarist&#x2019;s life that year after his wife Tracey suffered a postpartum psychotic episode following the birth of their son Andrew.

Wrung out from a grueling recording and touring schedule and increasingly debilitated by their drug habits, Andy and John Taylor made a lateral move into a new quartet, the Power Station, which also featured white-soul vocalist Robert Palmer and Chic&#x2019;s drummer Tony Thompson. Produced by Thompson&#x2019;s band mate Bernard Edwards, its self-titled 1985 debut reached No. 6 in the U.S. and No. 12 in the U.K. (A long-delayed 1996 sequel, with Edwards standing in on bass for John Taylor, then in rehab, failed to chart.)

By the time Duran Duran appeared at the U.S. incarnation of the transatlantic, internationally televised benefit concert Live Aid in July 1985, the original lineup of the group was reaching the end of its tether. Taylor wrote in his memoir, &#x201C;John and I were in a dark place&#x2026;.[W]e were dying inside. We were tired of twenty-four-hour attention, tired of drinking and taking drugs, haggard from the lifestyle we had once aspired to.&#x201D;

Exiting the band in 1986, Taylor attempted to clean up his life in Los Angeles and began working with Steve Jones, the former guitarist for the Sex Pistols and himself then newly in recovery. The fruits of their collaboration included &#x201C;Take It Easy,&#x201D; a No. 24 pop hit heard on the soundtrack for the film &#x201C;American Anthem,&#x201D; and the tough &#x201C;I Might Lie,&#x201D; which rose to No. 17 on Billboard&#x2019;s mainstream rock chart. His 1987 solo set &#x201C;Thunder&#x201D; reached No. 46 domestically. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid3' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Following occasional work behind Rod Stewart, Taylor rejoined Duran Duran, after an absence of 14 years, for a full reunion of the original band. A successful world tour and a new album, 2004&#x2019;s &#x201C;Astronaut&#x201D; (No. 3 in the U.K., No. 17 in the U.S.), followed. But the guitarist soon became discontent again, and exited a second time in 2006; material he had worked on for a new album was shelved.

&#x201C;I was tired of going over and over the same old creative difficulties and financial tensions,&#x201D; he later wrote, &#x201C;and I was fed up with having blazing rows with our management over what I perceived to be our lack of clear direction&#x2026;.We&#x2019;d ceased to function as a band; it was seriously dysfunctional. We&#x2019;d returned to being five individuals pulling in different directions, just as we&#x2019;d become in the eighties. When it came to sorting out our problems, just like before, we failed to connect.&#x201D;

In 2007-08, Taylor was briefly partnered in RockAffairs.com, a site devoted to the sale and promotion of music by unsigned independent artists.

He was born Feb. 16, 1961, in Tynemouth, Northumberland, and raised nearby Cullercoats.. At 11, he received his first guitar as a Christmas present, and in his teens played with local acts like the Gigolos before touring Europe.

He is survived by wife Tracey and his children Andrew, Isabelle, Bethany and Georgina.
